Within the $U_1$ leptoquark model, we investigate the decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, taking into account the constraints from $B 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ and $B 	o K^{(*)} 	au  ar{
u}$ decays. We find that the Wilson coefficients $C_{1,2}^{(\prime)}$ are highly constrained by the $B 	o K^{(*)} 	au  ar{
u}$ data, which in turn limits the allowed range of branching ratios and angular distributions for $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$. We also find that the $B 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay is more constrained than the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay, which is due to the fact that the former is more sensitive to the $C_2$ Wilson coefficient.
